course: dictionary
lesson: 5654
title: Listen: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Listen is a doing word, a verb. It can mean two different things. The first meaning is to pay attention to sounds or words so that you hear them. The second meaning is to take advice and do what someone says.
explain: The words around listen give you the clue. In «Listen for the main idea», the speaker wants you to pay close attention to the talk. In «He never listens!», the word means he does not do what he is told. Ask yourself: is this about hearing, or about obeying?
explain: Dolphins use listening to find things. «They send out fast clicks and listen to the echoes» means they pay close attention to sound coming back to them. Listening is about sound here, not about obeying anyone.
fact: Listen is a verb: listen, listens, listened, listening.
fact: To listen can mean to pay attention to sounds or words so that you hear them.
fact: To listen can also mean to take advice and do what someone says.
fact: Signal words like "first", "next" and "the most important thing" tell you when to listen closely.
fact: Sound travels well through water, which is why dolphins can listen for echoes even where it is too muddy to see far.
exercise: In «Listen for the main idea», what does listen mean? | To shout out the answer | To eat your lunch slowly | To leave the room quickly | *To pay attention to sounds or words so you hear them
exercise: «Dolphins send out fast clicks and listen to the echoes.» What are the dolphins doing? | Swimming away from the sea | *Paying attention to sound so they can find things | Singing a song for fun
exercise: «Adults usually know more, so listening to them is sensible.» What does listening to them mean here? | Hearing music on the radio | Ignoring them completely | *Taking their advice and doing what they say | Whispering back to them
test: «Listen for signal words like "first" and "next".» What should you pay attention to? | The weather outside | Your shoes | *Words that show the order of the ideas | Pictures on the wall
test: Grandma says, «Listening to her stories is a gift to both of you.» What does listen mean here? | To run fast around the garden | To write a letter to her | To leave her house quickly | *To pay attention to her words so you hear them
exam: Which meaning of listen is used in «He never listens!» when his mum tells him to tidy his room? | *To take advice and do what someone says | To send out fast clicks to find things | To hear the birds singing outside | To pay attention to music
